{"name":"Rosin","hex":"#39382f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Rosin","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Rosin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rosin","blocks":[{"text":"Rosin, also known as colophony or Greek pitch (Latin: pix graeca), is a resinous material obtained from pine trees and other plants, mostly conifers. The primary components of rosin are diterpenoids, i.e., C20 carboxylic acids. Rosin consists mainly of resin acids, especially abietic acid. Rosin often appears as a semi-transparent, brittle substance that ranges in color from yellow to black and melts at stove-top temperatures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Maison_du_patrimoine_de_Mimizan_colophane_2.jpg/330px-Maison_du_patrimoine_de_Mimizan_colophane_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosin","wikidata":"Q138937"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Kolophonium.jpg/500px-Kolophonium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Kolophonium.jpg/1280px-Kolophonium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Kolophonium.jpg/500px-Kolophonium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pharmaceutical rosin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKolophonium.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Plaque_et_resine.JPG/500px-Plaque_et_resine.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Plaque_et_resine.JPG/1280px-Plaque_et_resine.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","